From 6363d8b6d36db4ac13c8185567c37c407c016402 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hongchan Choi <hongchan@google.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:41:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [WebAudio] Construct MediaStreamAudioDestinationNode with
 options count

MediaStreamAudioDestinationNode::Create(context, options, ...)
previously constructed the node with kDefaultNumberOfChannels (2) before
calling setChannelCount(), causing the underlying
WebAudioMediaStreamSource to initialize with 2 channels. In addition,
MediaStreamAudioDestinationHandler::SetChannelCount() on the main thread
did not immediately update destination_consumer_->SetFormat().

This CL fixes both issues:
- Validate and pass options->channelCount() (bounded by
  kMaxChannelCountSupported = 8) directly to the
  MediaStreamAudioDestinationNode constructor.
- Update destination_consumer_->SetFormat() under consumer_lock_ inside
  MediaStreamAudioDestinationHandler::SetChannelCount().
- Add unit tests in MediaStreamAudioDestinationHandlerTest.

Fixed: 40711696
Change-Id: I86a0974a04f9335146c3929eae79923926be7f5d
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8468847
Commit-Queue: Hongchan Choi <hongchan@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Mahesh Kannan <kmaheshb@google.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1711759}
